###############################################################################
#                                                                             #
# This file is only meant to exclude broken dependency versions, not feature  #
# dependencies.                                                               #
#                                                                             #
# GUIDELINES:                                                                 #
#   1. Only list PyPI project versions that need to be excluded using `!=`    #
#      and `<`.                                                               #
#   2. It is allowed to have transitive dependency limitations in this file.  #
#   3. Apply bare minimum constraints under narrow conditions, use            #
#      environment markers if possible. E.g.  `; python_version < "3.12"`.    #
#   4. Whenever there are no constraints, let the file and this header        #
#      remain in Git.                                                         #
#                                                                             #
###############################################################################

# SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright © 2019, Sviatoslav Sydorenko

# NOTE: Metadata 2.5 support needs packaging 26.1. Twine 7.0 already
# NOTE: requires packaging >= 26.1 itself, so this floor is currently
# NOTE: redundant. It is kept to keep the requirement explicit, and to
# NOTE: guard against a future twine release declaring a lower bound
# NOTE: that is too low for the metadata version it emits support for,
# NOTE: which is what happened with twine 6.1 and metadata 2.4 below.
# Ref: https://github.com/pypa/twine/pull/1180
packaging >= 26.1
